<title>GERMANY: Buba revises up German July industry output.</title>
<headline>Buba revises up German July industry output.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank provided the following revised index figures for German industry output:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT	July 96	 June 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +0.8 (+0.2)    +0.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   -0.7 (-1.6)    -0.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    99.3 (98.7)    98.5</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +1.0 (+0.5)    +0.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   -1.1 (-1.7)    -0.9</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    96.3 (95.8)    95.3</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 -5.7 (-5.5)    +2.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   +3.5 (+3.7)    +5.3</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		   138.0 (138.2)  146.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted. The percentage change figures are calculated by Reuters from the indices. Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
